### 0. Login as admin
# @name loginAdmin
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@gmail.com",
  "password": "abc12345"
}

###

### 0b. Login as a regular customer for negative tests
# @name loginCustomer
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "farah@gmail.com",
  "password": "abc12345"
}

###

### 1. Create event as admin -> expect 201
# @name createEvent
POST http://localhost:8080/api/events
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Spring Boot Meetup",
  "description": "Monthly meetup for backend devs",
  "category": "Tech",
  "eventDate": "2026-09-15T18:00:00",
  "venue": "KL Convention Centre",
  "capacity": 50,
  "price": 0
}

###

### 2. Create event as customer -> expect 403
POST http://localhost:8080/api/events
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Should be blocked",
  "description": "Customers cannot create events",
  "category": "Tech",
  "eventDate": "2026-09-15T18:00:00",
  "venue": "Nowhere",
  "capacity": 10,
  "price": 0
}

###

### 3. List events as customer -> expect 200
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.token}}

###

### 4. List events, no token -> expect 401
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events

###

### 5. Get single event -> expect 200
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events/{{createEvent.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.token}}

###

### 6. Update event, shrink capacity below 0 booked -> expect 200 (nothing booked yet)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/events/{{createEvent.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Spring Boot Meetup",
  "description": "Monthly meetup for backend devs",
  "category": "Tech",
  "eventDate": "2026-09-15T18:00:00",
  "venue": "KL Convention Centre",
  "capacity": 30,
  "price": 0
}

###

### 7. Deactivate event as admin -> expect 204
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/events/{{createEvent.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}

###

### 8. Deactivate as customer -> expect 403
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/events/{{createEvent.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.token}}